WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.370
-This is a wonderful jacket.
I want to just start by saying.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:08.908
This is my -- listen, this --
I may never wear another thing.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I lost it, you know.
-I did know.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What happened?

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You saw it on the --
I -- I got so --

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.650 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I was at the airport,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:22.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I left it or dropped it
or someone took it.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.227 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You know people will.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.762 line:92%
-I know how they do it, yeah.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They see a jacket
and go, "Ooh."

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.300 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Got to have it."

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they could be big and --
but quicker than me.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.243 line:92%
-So I put it on Instagram.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That you lost it?

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Luckily, I had a thousand
pictures of it.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:47.881 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so I posted a picture
and said,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I lost my jacket in
Minneapolis/St. Paul airport."

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's my hometown.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Woo-hoo!
-Yeah.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, give it up
for Minneapolis.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:03.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Glad to see you got out here.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.500 line:92%
And I didn't get any response.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And then I said,

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Maybe I'll just call
the lost and found there."

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:15.375
Which don't -- You know how that
is, calling the lost and found.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:15.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.143 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-You never get through.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.578 line:92%
Boom, guy picks up, John.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Hey."
"Hey."

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.714 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You picked up.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
I turned into Romney there
for a second.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey!

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:28.922 line:92%
And I go, "Do you have --

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:32.258 size:84% position:42%
Can you check to see
if you have a giant --"

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.327 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the name of
that stuff they call it?

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:37.864 size:81% position:41% line:92%
There's a name for it.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:38.598 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Anyways, I think I said

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
herringbone which is wrong,
but jacket.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:46.172
And he comes back and he goes,
"We got a big blue checked one."

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:46.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.274 line:92%
I said, "Will you send it?"

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was, like, Thursday.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I said,
"Will you FedEx it to me?

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I'm on Seth's show --
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Monday and I'd like to
wear it."

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they did.
-And he did.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.454 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think his name
was Don Gubosch.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Don Gubosch.
Look there you are.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're so happy.
-Yeah.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's the FedEx box
and everything.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:09.729 line:92%
-You know, cause you need --

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.533
Nowadays, when you're going on
social media, you need a story.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.204
-It's obviously -- I'd just
gotten back from the new "Solo."

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
My "Star Wars" shirt.
-Gotcha.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I opened the package.
And what was in it?

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, that jacket.
It's obvious.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it's like --
-It's all wrinkled.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like a three-act play.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:34.087 size:84% position:42%
-Happiness is that I am
on Seth Meyers' show.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With your jacket.
-With my jacket!

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.757 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:38.958 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And Fred is back!

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fred's back.
-Yeah!

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:45.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What is --
You're on a newer tour.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the name of
your new tour?

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:47.901 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-"Big Underwear" tour.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.068 line:92%
-The "Big Underwear" tour.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:49.769 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How do you come up --

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.771
how do you name your tour
the "Big Underwear" tour?

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:55.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was washing my clothes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which I don't normally do.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when you're on the road,
you've got to do things.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I fold-- so I put them
in the dryer.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.751
And then I was folding them.
And I took out the underwear.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went, "Jesus."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did.
It was an involuntary "Jesus."

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like I go, "Jesus!"

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:17.130 size:81% position:41%
And I'm looking around
for someone to tell.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.631 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And no one was there.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:22.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Are these mine?!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.469 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"Are these mine?! No!"

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:26.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you don't know
how big your underwear on

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:29.309
while you're -- are while you're
putting them on.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got ahead of myself.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you don't know.
And then I go, "My God."

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.047 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so I said,
"I'm not -- I'm gonna do it.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna do a tour called
'Big Underwear' tour."

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:45.558
'Cause I'm an underwear hoarder.
I don't know if you know that.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.392 line:92%
-What are we talking? A total --

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:50.597
-Six big boxes when I cleaned
out my storage of big underwear.

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:51.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-From different decades.
-Oh, wow.

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'80s, '90s.
-So you've never --

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:56.302 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And looking back,

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.539
has the style changed a lot
over the last four decades?

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:00.373 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.674 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, yeah.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.077 line:92%
The '80s, they were carefree.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.378 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The '90s, ew.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, just --
yeah, they were.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:10.850 line:92%
You know, I was a poor kid.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I always think
I'm out of underwear.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:13.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, okay.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.154
-And that's why I had them all.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No one wants them either.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, have you tried to
give them away?

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:22.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Goodwill won't.
They shame you.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.396 line:92%
-They shamed you at Goodwill?

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
They go, "It's unsanitary."

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.100 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I go, "They're clean!"

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:27.700 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They were clean.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They won't take them?
-No.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I make artwork
out of them now.

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:32.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you -- obviously,
you play a mom,

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "Baskets",
which is fantastic.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a fantastic portrayal.
-Thank you.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.346 line:92%
-And did that inspire you

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
then to write this book
about your mom?

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:46.219 line:92%
-Yes. I came home one day.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.955
I was working on the show
with all my good friends.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:49.889 line:92%
There's Zach Galifianakis

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Jonathan Krisel
and Martha Kelly.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.893 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And I was overwhelmed.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.428 line:92%
And I was thinking about my mom.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I'm really
playing a mom.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not playing Louie Anderson
as a mom.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're really not.
-I'm not.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:02.568 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm telling you,

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:05.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
some weird thing happens to me
where I disappear.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:05.938 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It just does.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anyway, I can't explain it.
Wish I could.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I wrote, "Dear Mom,"
and I wrote this long letter.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.881 line:92%
And I sent it to a couple people

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it mattered to me,
the letter.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they -- they were --
both said,

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:26.726
my good friend Abraham and my
manager Amos, and they said

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:27.960 line:92%
this would make a good book.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Ugh, that seems
like a lot of work."

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:31.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your mom seemed to be quite
a character,

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:34.500 line:92%
especially at restaurants.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your mom like
at restaurants?

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, she didn't --
any Midwesterner,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:44.911
if they aren't waited on within
15 seconds, they do this.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:52.218 line:92%
"Is there anybody else here?"

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:52.719 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's true.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:55.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
Honestly, my mom's first words
were always,

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Could we get
some extra butter?"

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:59.525 line:92%
And the maitre d' would say,

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, let us seat
your party first."

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:09.235 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:10.870 line:92%
-It's really a lovely book.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:11.437 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she seemed like
a lovely woman.

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it really is truly,
for my money,

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:17.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the great portrayals
on television.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm so glad
you're still doing it.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you so much
for being back.

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:23.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just always so great
to see you.

